" ja'o ko dunda mi"

  I don't think ja'o really fits here.  I think you really want ".i se ni'i
bo" or ".i se ki'u bo"  (or if you prefer, "ni'i/ki'u lo du'u go'i kei ko
dunda mi") If I can't pay you for her, therefore give her to me. I'm not
sure what an evidential would mean in an imperative sentence.   Consider,
could you put e.g. "ti'e" there?  What would mean? Also, "mi" should be the
te dunda, not the se dunda.

     --gejyspa

